1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:04,637
# Countersign demo narration (draft, ~2:30 target)

2
00:00:04,637 --> 00:00:08,825
Shopping agents can spend money, but a card gives them your full authority.

3
00:00:08,825 --> 00:00:12,262
Countersign replaces that with a signed spending mandate.

4
00:00:12,262 --> 00:00:20,662
On the agent chat, the buyer states intent in plain language: buy the cheapest trail shoes you can find, under one hundred fifty dollars.

5
00:00:20,662 --> 00:00:26,200
The intent compiler turns that into explicit, signed constraints the buyer can review.

6
00:00:26,200 --> 00:00:31,112
When the agent tries to check out, the Gate evaluates the purchase against the mandate.

7
00:00:31,112 --> 00:00:37,850
For an allowed, in-budget item, the Gate returns ALLOW and creates a real PayPal sandbox order.

8
00:00:37,850 --> 00:00:46,437
The order is shown with its PayPal order ID and status CREATED and unpaid — a real third-party record, not a database mock.

9
00:00:46,437 --> 00:00:48,762
We can re-read it directly from PayPal.

10
00:00:48,762 --> 00:00:55,350
If a listing tries to break the rules — for example an injected or out-of-scope price — the Gate blocks it.

11
00:00:55,350 --> 00:00:58,500
The agent cannot spend outside the signed mandate.

12
00:00:58,500 --> 00:01:07,062
When a dispute is raised, the Dispute Defender runs a deterministic rule table, not a model, to decide whether to contest or refund.

13
00:01:07,062 --> 00:01:19,937
Here are two simulated dispute cases processed by the production pipeline: one unauthorized charge is contested with a cited evidence plan, and one agent-fault case is refunded because the agent bought the wrong thing.

14
00:01:19,937 --> 00:01:24,625
The contested case produces an evidence packet PDF with a QR code.

15
00:01:24,625 --> 00:01:38,337
Scanning it opens the public verifier, which recomputes checks from the packet itself and reports each result honestly — including what is simulated and what is skipped because no live signed chain is present in this demo fixture.

16
00:01:38,337 --> 00:01:46,437
Countersign makes agent payments provable: signed intent, enforced limits, real PayPal records, and evidence you can verify.

